  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Song of Solomon",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 6,
    "summary": "The song of love continues.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Whither is thy beloved gone, O thou fairest among women? whither is thy beloved turned aside? that we may seek him with thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "My beloved is gone down into his garden, to the beds of spices, to feed in the gardens, and to gather lilies.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I am my beloved’s, and my beloved is mine: he feedeth among the lilies.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 4
          },
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 36
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Thou art beautiful, O my love, as Tirzah, comely as Jerusalem, terrible as an army with banners.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 8
          },
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 82
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Turn away thine eyes from me, for they have overcome me: thy hair is as a flock of goats that appear from Gilead.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 68
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Thy teeth are as a flock of sheep which go up from the washing, whereof every one beareth twins, and there is not one barren among them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 13
          },
          {
            "start": 101,
            "end": 109
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "As a piece of a pomegranate are thy temples within thy locks.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 31
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "There are threescore queens, and fourscore concubines, and virgins without number.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "My dove, my undefiled is but one; she is the only one of her mother, she is the choice one of her that bare her. The daughters saw her, and blessed her; yea, the queens and the concubines, and they praised her.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 28
          },
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 40
          },
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 49
          },
          {
            "start": 73,
            "end": 75
          },
          {
            "start": 87,
            "end": 90
          },
          {
            "start": 153,
            "end": 157
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Who is she that looketh forth as the morning, fair as the moon, clear as the sun, and terrible as an army with banners?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 6
          },
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 15
          },
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 85
          },
          {
            "start": 98,
            "end": 105
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I went down into the garden of nuts to see the fruits of the valley, and to see whether the vine flourished, and the pomegranates budded.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 72
          },
          {
            "start": 109,
            "end": 112
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Or ever I was aware, my soul made me like the chariots of Amminadib.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 41
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Return, return, O Shulamite; return, return, that we may look upon thee. What will ye see in the Shulamite? As it were the company of two armies.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
  "nextChapterId": "songofsolomon7",
  "prevChapterId": "songofsolomon5",
  "volume": {
    "_id": "oldtestament",
    "title": "Old Testament",
    "titleShort": "OT",
    "titleOfficial": "The Old Testament"
  }
}